43	 *   - status INSTALLING → fetch + install the mod, then INSTALLED (or FAILED)
44	 *   - status REMOVING   → remove the mod, then delete the row (or FAILED)
45	 *
46	 * Wire into worker/index.ts handlers:  GAME_MOD_SYNC: gameModSync,
47	 *
48	 * ENGINE FAMILIES (2026-10-01 — minecraft, valheim, rust, cs2, factorio; see
49	 * lib/mods/installers/index.ts) go through lib/mods/engine.ts: verified
50	 * download, dependency resolution, safe placement, guest state file, rollback,
51	 * plus UPDATING / DISABLING / ENABLING. In SANDBOX they run the SAME pipeline
52	 * against a fake guest directory (lib/mods/guest-fs.ts LocalGuestFs) — real
53	 * downloads, real files, no simulated success.
54	 *
55	 * Every other family keeps the THREE PATHS below, mirroring game-config's
56	 * honesty guard so we never tell a customer a mod is installed when nothing
57	 * was written to their server:
58	 *  - SANDBOX: simulate (flip INSTALLING→INSTALLED, REMOVING→REMOVED). Dev only.
59	 *  - REAL (ENABLE_REAL_GAMEMODS=1, not sandbox): install/remove over SSH via the
60	 *    per-source adapter. Where an adapter isn't implemented yet, the mod is marked
61	 *    FAILED with a clear reason — never silently "INSTALLED".
62	 *  - Neither (production, flag off): mark the queued changes FAILED with a plain
63	 *    message. A change we did NOT apply is a failure and must say so.
64	 */
65	
66	const REAL_ENABLED = !SANDBOX && process.env.ENABLE_REAL_GAMEMODS === "1";
